[Music]  hey guys it's Jonah here who loves a  good pokeball it is currently my  favorite dinner if you have no idea what  a pokeball is you are missing out and  you need to start adding this dish into  your meals so be sure to watch this  video through okay so pokeball is a  traditional Hawaiian dish typically  served with raw fish slices rise lots of  vegetables and other toppings such as  avocado mango nuts and seeds and more so  it is nutritious and delicious the best  part about pokeball is that you can keep  changing the ingredients according to  your liking and also your mood so here  are five steps to make a really healthy  pokeball so the first step is to choose  your base it can either be brown rice  sushi rice quinoa couscous or even  noodles the second step is to pick your  protein it can either be salmon tuna  prawns or for vegans you can go for tofu  and the third step is to pack on the  vegetables and also fruits such as  lettuce cabbage cucumber cherry tomatoes  avocado mango and more so pack as many  varieties of vegetables as you want the  next step is to add the toppings such as  sesame seeds scallions onions and nuts  and seeds of your choice and the final  step is to drizzle the sauce to really  pack in the flavors so I'm going to  share with you three of my favorite  pokeball recipes salmon sashimi on wild  rice salty prawns on glass noodles and  of course we need a vegan option  marinated tofu on quinoa so let's start  by making the sauce which will be used  for all three recipes so in a bowl mix  in 1 tablespoon of soy sauce 1/2 a  teaspoon of rice wine vinegar and about  half a tablespoon of fresh lemon juice  and set aside let's start with the  salmon sashimi on wild rice what you'll  need are 1 cup of cooked rice I used  wild rice about 1/3 cup of raw salmon  cut into cubes quarter of an avocado cut  into cubes quarter cup of steamed  edamame  quarter cup of mango cut into cubes we  want to start by marinating the salmon  so in a small bowl mix in the soy sauce  sesame oil and sesame seeds then pour  the sauce on to the salmon coat and let  it sit for about 15 minutes  then all you have to do is assemble the  dish in a bowl so always start with a  base which is the rice and arrange the  rest of the ingredients finally drizzle  with a little bit of sauce and serve  just look at this dish guys it is  colorful it's packed with all the good  stuff and is so flavoursome this One  Bowl has about 465 calories I would be  happy to eat this every single day so  the next recipe is the sauteed prawns on  glass noodles what you'll need are 80  grams of glass noodles 1/3 cup of prawns  peeled cut a cup of cabbage shredded  quarter cup of cherry tomatoes 1/2 2  tablespoons of cucumber sliced 1  tablespoon of toasted seaweed shredded  and half a tablespoon of sesame oil  let's start by prepping the noodles in a  large bowl place the noodles and pour  enough boiling water over the noodles  then just cover with a plate and let it  soak for about 10 to 15 minutes until  the noodles are soft and just drain the  water off in a small bowl makes a  dessert sauce rice vinegar garlic and  sesame seeds and pour the mixture over  the prawns and allow the prawns to  marinate for about 5 minutes next heat  the sesame oil over medium-high heat  then add the marinated prawns and cook  very quickly just for about 4 to 5  minutes until the prawns are pink don't  overcook them it's time to assemble the  dish again always start with the base  which is the glass noodles and arrange  the rest of the ingredients your prawns  your vegetables and your toppings  finally drizzle with a little bit of  sauce and serve so this one Bowl has  about 443 calories  for the vegetarians and vegans out there  this final recipe is for you so for the  marinated tofu on quinoa what you'll  need are 1 cup of quinoa cooked about  1/3 block of firm tofu drained and cut  into cubes quarter of an avocado cut  into cubes cut a cup of carrot shredded  2 tablespoons of corn and about 2  tablespoons of cucumber sliced so again  let's start by marinating the tofu in a  small bowl combine the soy sauce sesame  oil garlic sesame seeds and red pepper  flakes coat the tofu and leave it to  marinate for about five to 10 minutes  and it's my favorite part again time to  put this dish together so we've got the  quinoa tofu and all the vegetables hold  the sauce mixture and sprinkle with more  sesame seeds and serve this one ball has  about 435 calories all these recipes  will keep you full for a long period of  time and it will give you the energy to  keep going so the great thing is you can  keep experimenting with different  ingredients different base and different  protein so you won't feel bored eating  the same thing over and over again so I  don't want to hear that healthy food is  boring alright so each Bowl is packed  with complex carbs clean protein healthy  fat and lots of vegetables how do you  like your pokeball let me know in the  comments below be sure to try this  recipe out because I trust you will be  hooked ok do take pictures of your  creation and share them with me on  Facebook and Instagram tag me at  Jonassen official and hashtag chase of  recipes because I want to see all your  healthy pokeballs  do also like this video share this video  and subscribe to my youtube channel for  a lot more healthy recipes workout  videos and also fitness tips guys do you  also turn on your notification button so  that you will get notified every time I  upload a new video all the best

